Follow-up to karr #33, which landed the generated Kind -> plural table in IO::K8s::Role::APIObject (maint/spec-resource-plural-gen.pl, keyed "$api_version/$Kind").

The table is generated from the collection REST paths of spec/v1.36.3.json, so it only contains GVKs upstream v1.36 actually serves. 15 shipped classes sit on older tracks that upstream has since dropped, so they get no key and resource_plural() returns undef:

    admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1alpha1  ValidatingAdmissionPolicy, ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding
    admissionregistration.k8s.io/v1beta1   ValidatingAdmissionPolicy, ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding
    authentication.k8s.io/v1alpha1         SelfSubjectReview
    authentication.k8s.io/v1beta1          SelfSubjectReview
    coordination.k8s.io/v1alpha1           LeaseCandidate
    flowcontrol.apiserver.k8s.io/v1beta3   FlowSchema, PriorityLevelConfiguration
    resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3               DeviceClass, ResourceClaim, ResourceClaimTemplate, ResourceSlice
    storage.k8s.io/v1alpha1                VolumeAttributesClass
    storagemigration.k8s.io/v1alpha1       StorageVersionMigration

Every one of them has a same-group sibling in a served version whose plural IS in the table (validatingadmissionpolicies, selfsubjectreviews, leasecandidates, flowschemas, resourceclaims, volumeattributesclasses, storageversionmigrations, ...).

Not fixed in #33 on purpose: the exact-GVK key is fail-closed, matching the karr #17/#31 precedent that expand_class never substitutes a class that cannot confirm the requested version. Downstream is no worse off than before #33 (it was undef for everything).

Possible fix, if wanted: a second generated tier keyed "$group|$Kind", emitted only for group+Kind pairs where every version in the spec agrees on the plural. That is still upstream data, not a heuristic -- the plural is a property of the GroupResource, which is what RBAC addresses, and the version never varies it. The generator would assert the agreement and die otherwise (it already dies on same-key conflicts). Cost: ~78 extra table entries plus one fallback lookup.

Note the design constraint in #33 was explicitly "group+version+Kind, not the bare Kind"; a group+Kind tier meets the disambiguation intent (core Event vs events.k8s.io Event stay distinct) but is a deliberate widening and needs a call from the maintainer.

Also undef, and correctly so (not part of this ticket): the 3 subresources (Eviction, Scale, TokenRequest) and the 7 embedded *TemplateSpec / *Template types, which have no GVK and never appear as a "kind:" on the wire.
Implemented, uncommitted, left in the tree for the maintainer's lane (Changes + commit not touched).

Second tier landed as %RESOURCE_PLURAL_BY_GROUP in lib/IO/K8s/Role/APIObject.pm, keyed "$group|$Kind" ('' group for core), consulted only when the exact "$api_version/$Kind" lookup misses. maint/spec-resource-plural-gen.pl emits both tables from one run into two separately delimited generated blocks and dies if two versions of one group claim different plurals for one Kind.

Numbers against spec/v1.36.3.json: 95 tier-1 entries (unchanged), 76 tier-2 entries. Shipped upstream APIObject classes 120: 110 now carry a plural, up from 95. The agreement assertion never fired on the real spec (0 disagreements); verified it is live by running the generator against a synthetic spec with a deliberate v1/v1beta1 plural mismatch, which dies as intended.

Still undef, by design: the 3 subresources (Eviction, Scale, TokenRequest, filtered out by trailing path segment so neither tier can reach them) and the 7 embedded template types (PodTemplateSpec, PersistentVolumeClaimTemplate, JobTemplateSpec, ResourceClaimTemplateSpec x4 - no GVK at all).

t/51_resource_plural.t extended to 12 subtests: the 15 classes resolving, each against its served sibling; core Event vs events.k8s.io Event still distinct; a synthetic IO::K8s::Api::Batch::V1alpha9::Ingress tripwire that must stay undef (a bare-Kind fallback would hand it 'ingresses'); the full 120-class coverage guard with the exact 10-item miss list. The old #33 assertion 'resource.k8s.io/v1alpha3 ResourceClaim -> undef' was the one claim replaced, deliberately.

